## 3. Parsing and Validation in Dart

To prevent invalid or malformed configuration files from being loaded, we implement a Dart parser using the `xml` package.

### Validation Checklist

1. **API Key Verification:** Ensure `apiKey` exists and is non-empty.
2. **Timeout Boundaries:** Verify `timeout` is an integer between `10` and `60` seconds.
3. **Unique User IDs:** Validate that all `<user>` elements possess unique `id` attributes.
4. **Firewall Rule Actions:** Ensure every `<rule>` action strictly evaluates to `allow` or `deny`.

### Complete Dart Implementation

Add the `xml` package to your `pubspec.yaml`:

```yaml
dependencies:
  xml: ^6.3.0

```

`main.dart`:

```dart
import 'package:xml/xml.dart';

void main() {
  final String xmlString = '''
<appConfig>
  <environment>
    <mode value="production" />
    <api>
      <baseUrl>https://api.holberton.com</baseUrl>
      <apiKey>ABCD1234-EFGH5678-IJKL9101</apiKey>
      <timeout>30</timeout>
    </api>
  </environment>

  <permissions>
    <permission name="location" required="true" />
    <permission name="storage" required="false" />
    <permission name="camera" required="false" />
  </permissions>

  <users>
    <user id="1" role="admin">
      <name>John Doe</name>
      <email>johndoe@holberton.com</email>
      <preferences>
        <language>en</language>
        <theme>dark</theme>
        <notifications enabled="true" />
      </preferences>
    </user>
    <user id="2" role="viewer">
      <name>Jane Smith</name>
      <email>janesmith@holberton.com</email>
      <preferences>
        <language>fr</language>
        <theme>light</theme>
        <notifications enabled="false" />
      </preferences>
    </user>
  </users>

  <security>
    <encryption>
      <type>AES-256</type>
      <key>Base64EncodedEncryptionKey==</key>
    </encryption>
    <firewall>
      <rules>
        <rule action="allow" ip="192.168.1.0/24" />
        <rule action="deny" ip="0.0.0.0/0" />
      </rules>
    </firewall>
  </security>

  <features>
    <feature name="betaTesting" enabled="true" />
    <feature name="chat" enabled="false" />
    <feature name="fileSharing" enabled="true" />
  </features>
</appConfig>
''';

  try {
    validateAppConfig(xmlString);
    print('SUCCESS: XML configuration parsed and validated successfully.');
  } catch (e) {
    print('VALIDATION ERROR: $e');
  }
}

void validateAppConfig(String xmlRaw) {
  final document = XmlDocument.parse(xmlRaw);
  final root = document.getElement('appConfig');

  if (root == null) {
    throw Exception('Missing root element <appConfig>');
  }

  // 1. Ensure the apiKey is not empty
  final apiKeyElement = root.findAllElements('apiKey').firstOrNull;
  if (apiKeyElement == null || apiKeyElement.innerText.trim().isEmpty) {
    throw Exception('Validation Failed: <apiKey> is missing or empty.');
  }

  // 2. Check that timeout is within an acceptable range (10-60 seconds)
  final timeoutElement = root.findAllElements('timeout').firstOrNull;
  if (timeoutElement == null) {
    throw Exception('Validation Failed: <timeout> element is missing.');
  }
  
  final timeoutVal = int.tryParse(timeoutElement.innerText.trim());
  if (timeoutVal == null || timeoutVal < 10 || timeoutVal > 60) {
    throw Exception(
      'Validation Failed: <timeout> must be an integer between 10 and 60 seconds. Got: ${timeoutElement.innerText}',
    );
  }

  // 3. Verify all user elements have unique id attributes
  final userElements = root.findAllElements('user');
  final Set<String> userIds = {};

  for (final user in userElements) {
    final idAttr = user.getAttribute('id');
    if (idAttr == null || idAttr.trim().isEmpty) {
      throw Exception('Validation Failed: Found <user> element without an "id" attribute.');
    }
    if (userIds.contains(idAttr)) {
      throw Exception('Validation Failed: Duplicate user ID detected: "$idAttr".');
    }
    userIds.add(idAttr);
  }

  // 4. Validate firewall rules rule actions (allow/deny) are implemented correctly
  final ruleElements = root.findAllElements('rule');
  final allowedActions = {'allow', 'deny'};

  for (final rule in ruleElements) {
    final action = rule.getAttribute('action');
    if (action == null || !allowedActions.contains(action.toLowerCase())) {
      throw Exception(
        'Validation Failed: Invalid firewall rule action "$action". Must be "allow" or "deny".',
      );
    }
  }
}

```

---

## 4. Conclusion

Static XML configurations can pose significant risks in mobile development if treated as secure storage. Hardcoded secrets, permissive rule declarations, and unvalidated parameters leave applications exposed to decompilation and exploitation.

By combining proper secrets management (using OS Keychains/Keystores) with strict input validation frameworks during application startup, developers can ensure application integrity and safeguard sensitive user data.
